A||||5||Jaei Sun||Rear window q's||||1||
Z||000000||Jaei Sun||11-18-2000||07:21 PM||||I was wondering for the cars without rear defrost how often does it get fogged up/moisture on the inside of the back window?<P>And sometime in the future if I would add the Defroster I know I would need the window, the wiring, the switch and the relay... is there anything else to it??<P>And in a releated matter does anyone know if the Honda Del Sols have rear defrost?  I heard that the back window is removeable and if that's true how would the rear deforst work?  Do you have to like unplug/plug in the window upon removal/installation?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rodrv6||11-18-2000||08:47 PM||||I don't have a rear defroster on my 84, and I really have never seen a time when I needed it.  The heat from the engine seems to warm up the window quite well!  Of course, I live down south and winters aren't near as severe as where you are, but I've never missed not having it.  I think the hardest part about installing one would be changing the rear window.  Haven't done it myself, but other posts on the forum indicate that it is a real pain!<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-18-2000||09:02 PM||||It clears pretty fast with the defog off. A little faster if it's on. I've never had it fog once the car has been running unless it was raining like hell when I got in. Then the whole car fogs in about 2 sec.<P>The winshield defroster is capable of throwing so much air that rear defog doesn't get used much in my car. Usually just first thing in the morning when I have to see to back out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||deceler8||11-19-2000||09:50 AM||||Never fogs, never ices...<P>1986 2m4...no defrost. And that's here in the Upper Midwest where -20 is pretty routine.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||11-19-2000||09:57 AM||||DelSol rear window is not removable. It is a power window just like one on a door.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Standard||11-19-2000||07:15 PM||||The rear window doesn't fog on the inside, it fogs on the outside.  As soon as it starts getting cold out, I use my defrost every time I start my car.  With my 84 it would usually take 5-10 minutes for the window to clear up, I didn't have r. defrost on it.  I usually only need it the first time I start my car in the day, or after it's been sitting for a few hours.  Some people don't believe me, but it really helps.<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||1
